{
  "name": "Muyi Zhu",
  "bioHtml": "Muyi Zhu is currently a Research Assistant in the Department of Geography at the University of Hong Kong, supervised by <a href=\"https://geog.hku.hk/js-xu\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><strong>Prof. Junshi Xu</strong></a>. Muyi is expected to begin his PhD studies at ETH Zurich in January 2027, under the supervision of <a href=\"https://im.ibi.ethz.ch/en/people/prof-dr-bryan-adey.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><strong>Prof. Bryan T. Adey</strong></a>.\nHis research focuses on road safety, environmental exposure, and active urban mobility, with a particular emphasis on evaluating the effectiveness of infrastructure interventions for pedestrians, cyclists, and micromobility users. He applies geospatial modelling, machine learning, and causal inference to assess how infrastructure and built-environment interventions affect actual and perceived safety.\nMuyi Zhu received a B.Eng. in Urban and Rural Planning from <a href=\"https://sola.bjfu.edu.cn/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><strong>Beijing Forestry University</strong></a> in 2024 and an MSc in Geospatial Data Science from <a href=\"https://geog.hku.hk/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><strong>the University of Hong Kong</strong></a> in 2025.",
  "interests": [
    "My key research interests include:",
    "Road Safety",
    "Infrastructure Evaluation",
    "Spatiotemporal Urban Mobility",
    "Air Quality Modeling"
  ],
